99,"scaruffi":null},{"id":170088453171885,"name":"Scaruffi 1960s","src":"charts","grp":"Scaruffi","list_year":null,"rank":76,"year":1966,"note":null,"total":207,"scaruffi":null},{"id":4389278164509,"name":"Music Genre Tree","src":"musthear","grp":"musicbrainz","list_year":null,"rank":662,"year":null,"note":null,"total":1042,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Released shortly before Sgt. Pepper's, *Pet Sounds* by The Beach Boys was seen by The Beatles as an absolute reference for creative quality and represented a significant departure from their own work at the time. It became the maximum idea of creative quality for the band. \"Para ellos era la absoluta referencia, la máxima idea de calidad creativa que podía tener a alguien.\"","year":1966,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Así se grabó el Sgt. Pepper's","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cDrTT4b-2gQ"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album is credited with inaugurating the golden age of psychedelia, even if it didn't invent the genre itself. It featured complex recording processes developed by Brian Wilson. \"el Pet Sounds inauguraba, posiblemente no inauguraba la psicodelia, pero sí inauguraba la época dorada de la psicodelia.\"","year":1966,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Así se grabó el Sgt. Pepper's","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cDrTT4b-2gQ"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album, released in 1966, is cited by some emo researchers as a starting point for emo music. This theory considers the record's lyrical themes, Brian Wilson's song construction, and his emotionally damaged state at the time of its creation as evidence for its early emo attributes. \"some emo researchers, and there are such things, say that emo began with the beach boys and the pet sounds album in 1966, which is not really crazy if you look at the record's lyrical themes, how Brian Wilson constructed the songs, and the fact that he was so emotionally damaged at the time.\"","year":1966,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alt Rock Revivals Part 3: Emo","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v_am7ifh7Pk"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album, released in 1966, was described as a masterpiece that elevated Brian Wilson to the stature of a genius, carving an exciting new path for music alongside The Beatles' Rubber Soul. Before its release, The Beach Boys were known for adolescent hits about surfing, Californian girls, and cars. Inspired by Rubber Soul, Wilson created a deeply introspective and stimulating album, introducing orchestral arrangements and unusual sounds that challenged the pop and rock conventions of the time, with lyrics exploring profound themes like love, loss, and the search for meaning. \"En 1966 vio la Luz Petzhounds de los Beach Boys, una obra maestra que lebo a Bryan Wilson a la altura de Gienio y Cabrío, junto con Raver Soul de los Beatles, un nuevo exitante camino para la música.\"","year":1966,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Central Sonora","episode":"El Álbum Perdido que pudo cambiar la música ｜ Smile de The Beach Boys","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DlVClI89yn4"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Creative Quality Reference","body":"Released shortly before Sgt. Pepper's, *Pet Sounds* by The Beach Boys was seen by The Beatles as an absolute reference for creative quality and represented a significant departure from their own work at the time. It became the maximum idea of creative quality for the band. \"Para ellos era la absoluta referencia, la máxima idea de calidad creativa que podía tener a alguien.\"","year":1966,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Así se grabó el Sgt. Pepper's","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cDrTT4b-2gQ"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Psychedelia Golden Age","body":"This album is credited with inaugurating the golden age of psychedelia, even if it didn't invent the genre itself. It featured complex recording processes developed by Brian Wilson. \"el Pet Sounds inauguraba, posiblemente no inauguraba la psicodelia, pero sí inauguraba la época dorada de la psicodelia.\"","year":1966,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Así se grabó el Sgt. Pepper's","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cDrTT4b-2gQ"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":201729344438070,"artist":"The Beach Boys","artist_id":250434572201079,"title":"Pet Sounds","year":1966,"ess":0,"yt":"dndX7D2Chg8","kind":null,"book":{"id":1,"title":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded","author":"Jon Savage","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/"},"scene":"The Beach Boys y Brian Wilson","scene_id":199959870211854,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/#beach-boys","chapters":["Noviembre: Good Vibrations: Motown y el soul en Reino Unido, los Beach Boys y el Sunset Strip"],"pages":[]},{"id":201729344438070,"artist":"Beach Boys","artist_id":250434572201079,"title":"Pet Sounds","year":1966,"ess":1,"yt":"eacses-JhsM","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"El diluvio: invasión británica y garage","scene_id":245539326529376,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#british-invasion","chapters":["Sección 2.5"],"pages":[[1,23,null]]},{"id":201729344438070,"artist":"The Beach Boys","artist_id":250434572201079,"title":"Pet Sounds","year":1966,"ess":0,"yt":"dndX7D2Chg8","kind":null,"book":{"id":10,"title":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/"},"scene":"Art-rock","scene_id":191826593279813,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#art-rock","chapters":["Cap. 21: Apéndice 2 · El salto cuántico: avances exponenciales en la tecnología musical (1836-2017)"],"pages":[[1,425]]},{"id":201729344438070,"artist":"Beach Boys